{"duration_api_ms":985222,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"765ef8e5-7325-498a-b040-3b7ca38cdf8d","total_cost_usd":4.275341600000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":169827,"cache_read_input_tokens":13971838,"output_tokens":80125,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":43906},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":169827,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2712,"cache_read_input_tokens":192918,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1240},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":208,"outputTokens":80125,"cacheReadInputTokens":13971838,"cacheCreationInputTokens":169827,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":4.275341600000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":43906,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":138,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Implemented an Ansible-driven WireGuard gateway: node1 (VyOS) terminates a WireGuard tunnel to node3; node1 NATs (masquerades) tunnel traffic toward node2; node2 runs the demo app on TCP 8080 behind a firewalld rule that only accepts connections from node1's LAN IP. node3 can reach node2:8080 only via the tunnel (direct access is rejected by node2's firewall). All work was orchestrated from node4, the pre-configured Ansible control node, using an idempotent playbook at /root/wireguard-gateway/playbooks/site.yml. All 4 nodes were restarted one at a time with proven boot-id changes and confirmed post-restart recovery.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed topology: node1=VyOS gateway (10.100.165.10), node2/node3=AlmaLinux9 (10.100.165.11/.12), node4=Ubuntu Ansible control node (10.100.165.13) with pre-installed ansible-core and its own SSH keypair\",\"Bootstrapped SSH access from node4 to node2/node3 root authorized_keys, and to node1's vyos user; after discovering VyOS regenerates authorized_keys from committed config on boot, re-did the node1 key via VyOS's declarative `set system login user vyos authentication public-keys` so it survives reboots\",\"Wrote an Ansible inventory (inventory/hosts.ini) and playbook (playbooks/site.yml) on node4: generates WireGuard keypairs on node1 and node3; configures the VyOS wg0 interface, peer, and a NAT source-masquerade rule (wg subnet -> node2) via the script-template/configure/commit/save envelope; writes wg0.conf and enables wg-quick@wg0 on node3; deploys a python3 http.server app on port 8080 as a systemd unit on node2 plus a firewalld rich rule restricting port 8080 to node1's LAN address\",\"Diagnosed a VyOS-specific bug: running configure/set/commit as the unprivileged vyos SSH user silently fails ('without config session') because the config-session mount context isn't established for a plain user shell; fixed by enabling Ansible become (sudo to root) for the gateway host, which vyos has passwordless sudo for\",\"Verified end-to-end: node3 reaches node2:8080 through the wg0 tunnel; after manually removing the tunnel-specific /32 route on node3, direct access to node2:8080 fails (connection refused/no route), proving the tunnel is the only path; restored the route via wg-quick and reconfirmed connectivity\",\"Captured healthy baselines (boot_id, uptime, service/tunnel/app state) on all 4 nodes, then restarted them one at a time (node1, node2, node3, node4) via native reboot, polling until each came back, confirming a changed boot_id each time, and re-verifying service health, WireGuard tunnel state, NAT config persistence, firewalld rule persistence, and full tunnel connectivity after each restart\",\"Re-ran the Ansible playbook after all restarts to confirm idempotency (no unintended changes) and working SSH connectivity to all managed nodes\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Application served from node2 on TCP 8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-819f6fe136be4a3a\",\"cmd-4f99f2b4b3de4f25\",\"cmd-b306023319f34b3e\"],\"summary\":\"systemd unit wg-demo-app.service runs python3 http.server on 0.0.0.0:8080 on node2; content served and confirmed reachable\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 reaches the app only through a WireGuard tunnel terminated on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0805e8f0fa8b484c\",\"cmd-b306023319f34b3e\",\"cmd-3c609693529e47e9\",\"cmd-405366519ce548f0\"],\"summary\":\"wg0 on node1 shows an established peer/handshake with node3; node3's curl to node2:8080 succeeds over the wg0-routed path; after deleting the tunnel-specific route, direct access from node3's real IP fails with 'No route to host' (firewalld reject), and access is restored once the wg0 route returns\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implementation via Ansible from the control node\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b6c44ff620134fb8\",\"cmd-f3e7554c10fa4578\",\"cmd-45b761a9ff6543c3\",\"cmd-ba8a14d709904138\",\"cmd-d7422d1829f2425b\"],\"summary\":\"Inventory and playbook authored and executed from node4 (the designated control_node with ansible-core installed); playbook applies all WireGuard/NAT/app/firewall configuration across node1/node2/node3 and re-runs idempotently\"},{\"requirement\":\"VyOS config-session bug diagnosis and fix\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e246c02ac37e4396\",\"cmd-9798dd118af84b64\",\"cmd-0805e8f0fa8b484c\"],\"summary\":\"Isolated the failure to the vyos user's SSH session lacking a valid config session; confirmed sudo/root context resolves it, then wired become:true into the gateway play, producing a clean 'no configuration changes to commit' / successful apply\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart evidence (baseline, restart ack, changed boot id, recovery)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-72c06d1d8eea40c9\",\"cmd-83f37dca0a9a4267\",\"cmd-3487766403db4c40\",\"cmd-a6404c14edbb4be0\",\"cmd-840c859b25fb4f92\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 01e92881...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id c5b68ddb... with 22s uptime; wg0 interface, peer config, and NAT rule all intact post-restart; node3 tunnel access confirmed working after node1 restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart evidence (baseline, restart ack, changed boot id, recovery)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-657049fe43a84fd5\",\"cmd-0399457673844d04\",\"cmd-09bd86ac820d4f2b\",\"cmd-dcf0124996c1448e\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id f54d7366...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id a7d3bc82... with 4s uptime; wg-demo-app.service active and firewalld rich rule intact post-restart, app responds locally\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart evidence (baseline, restart ack, changed boot id, recovery)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2a318138972c4b24\",\"cmd-b5aea230d9234c17\",\"cmd-0e2962c15a6c49e5\",\"cmd-338a1e9588f04d53\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id dfdea52d...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id 1bb5c3ca... with 5s uptime; wg-quick@wg0 active, tunnel route restored automatically, app reachable through the tunnel post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 (control node) restart evidence (baseline, restart ack, changed boot id, recovery)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0accca332f444e68\",\"cmd-20d4e6514bb54f82\",\"cmd-d085832a9f54471c\",\"cmd-d7422d1829f2425b\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id e796da36...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id 86d29d70... with 4s uptime; ansible-playbook and project files intact, playbook re-run against all managed nodes succeeded post-restart\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Implemented an Ansible-driven WireGuard gateway: node1 (VyOS) terminates a WireGuard tunnel to node3; node1 NATs (masquerades) tunnel traffic toward node2; node2 runs the demo app on TCP 8080 behind a firewalld rule that only accepts connections from node1's LAN IP. node3 can reach node2:8080 only via the tunnel (direct access is rejected by node2's firewall). All work was orchestrated from node4, the pre-configured Ansible control node, using an idempotent playbook at /root/wireguard-gateway/playbooks/site.yml. All 4 nodes were restarted one at a time with proven boot-id changes and confirmed post-restart recovery.","actions_performed":["Surveyed topology: node1=VyOS gateway (10.100.165.10), node2/node3=AlmaLinux9 (10.100.165.11/.12), node4=Ubuntu Ansible control node (10.100.165.13) with pre-installed ansible-core and its own SSH keypair","Bootstrapped SSH access from node4 to node2/node3 root authorized_keys, and to node1's vyos user; after discovering VyOS regenerates authorized_keys from committed config on boot, re-did the node1 key via VyOS's declarative `set system login user vyos authentication public-keys` so it survives reboots","Wrote an Ansible inventory (inventory/hosts.ini) and playbook (playbooks/site.yml) on node4: generates WireGuard keypairs on node1 and node3; configures the VyOS wg0 interface, peer, and a NAT source-masquerade rule (wg subnet -> node2) via the script-template/configure/commit/save envelope; writes wg0.conf and enables wg-quick@wg0 on node3; deploys a python3 http.server app on port 8080 as a systemd unit on node2 plus a firewalld rich rule restricting port 8080 to node1's LAN address","Diagnosed a VyOS-specific bug: running configure/set/commit as the unprivileged vyos SSH user silently fails ('without config session') because the config-session mount context isn't established for a plain user shell; fixed by enabling Ansible become (sudo to root) for the gateway host, which vyos has passwordless sudo for","Verified end-to-end: node3 reaches node2:8080 through the wg0 tunnel; after manually removing the tunnel-specific /32 route on node3, direct access to node2:8080 fails (connection refused/no route), proving the tunnel is the only path; restored the route via wg-quick and reconfirmed connectivity","Captured healthy baselines (boot_id, uptime, service/tunnel/app state) on all 4 nodes, then restarted them one at a time (node1, node2, node3, node4) via native reboot, polling until each came back, confirming a changed boot_id each time, and re-verifying service health, WireGuard tunnel state, NAT config persistence, firewalld rule persistence, and full tunnel connectivity after each restart","Re-ran the Ansible playbook after all restarts to confirm idempotency (no unintended changes) and working SSH connectivity to all managed nodes"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Application served from node2 on TCP 8080","command_ids":["cmd-819f6fe136be4a3a","cmd-4f99f2b4b3de4f25","cmd-b306023319f34b3e"],"summary":"systemd unit wg-demo-app.service runs python3 http.server on 0.0.0.0:8080 on node2; content served and confirmed reachable"},{"requirement":"node3 reaches the app only through a WireGuard tunnel terminated on node1","command_ids":["cmd-0805e8f0fa8b484c","cmd-b306023319f34b3e","cmd-3c609693529e47e9","cmd-405366519ce548f0"],"summary":"wg0 on node1 shows an established peer/handshake with node3; node3's curl to node2:8080 succeeds over the wg0-routed path; after deleting the tunnel-specific route, direct access from node3's real IP fails with 'No route to host' (firewalld reject), and access is restored once the wg0 route returns"},{"requirement":"Implementation via Ansible from the control node","command_ids":["cmd-b6c44ff620134fb8","cmd-f3e7554c10fa4578","cmd-45b761a9ff6543c3","cmd-ba8a14d709904138","cmd-d7422d1829f2425b"],"summary":"Inventory and playbook authored and executed from node4 (the designated control_node with ansible-core installed); playbook applies all WireGuard/NAT/app/firewall configuration across node1/node2/node3 and re-runs idempotently"},{"requirement":"VyOS config-session bug diagnosis and fix","command_ids":["cmd-e246c02ac37e4396","cmd-9798dd118af84b64","cmd-0805e8f0fa8b484c"],"summary":"Isolated the failure to the vyos user's SSH session lacking a valid config session; confirmed sudo/root context resolves it, then wired become:true into the gateway play, producing a clean 'no configuration changes to commit' / successful apply"},{"requirement":"node1 restart evidence (baseline, restart ack, changed boot id, recovery)","command_ids":["cmd-72c06d1d8eea40c9","cmd-83f37dca0a9a4267","cmd-3487766403db4c40","cmd-a6404c14edbb4be0","cmd-840c859b25fb4f92"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 01e92881...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id c5b68ddb... with 22s uptime; wg0 interface, peer config, and NAT rule all intact post-restart; node3 tunnel access confirmed working after node1 restart"},{"requirement":"node2 restart evidence (baseline, restart ack, changed boot id, recovery)","command_ids":["cmd-657049fe43a84fd5","cmd-0399457673844d04","cmd-09bd86ac820d4f2b","cmd-dcf0124996c1448e"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id f54d7366...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id a7d3bc82... with 4s uptime; wg-demo-app.service active and firewalld rich rule intact post-restart, app responds locally"},{"requirement":"node3 restart evidence (baseline, restart ack, changed boot id, recovery)","command_ids":["cmd-2a318138972c4b24","cmd-b5aea230d9234c17","cmd-0e2962c15a6c49e5","cmd-338a1e9588f04d53"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id dfdea52d...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id 1bb5c3ca... with 5s uptime; wg-quick@wg0 active, tunnel route restored automatically, app reachable through the tunnel post-restart"},{"requirement":"node4 (control node) restart evidence (baseline, restart ack, changed boot id, recovery)","command_ids":["cmd-0accca332f444e68","cmd-20d4e6514bb54f82","cmd-d085832a9f54471c","cmd-d7422d1829f2425b"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id e796da36...; reboot acknowled